USB-to-UART Converter PCB

Project Overview

A USB-to-UART converter PCB designed using KiCad to provide serial communication between a computer and a UART-based microcontroller or embedded system.

Key Features

- USB interface for computer connectivity
- UART TX/RX communication
- USB power input
- USB data-line protection
- Compact PCB layout
- SMD component-based design
- Ground plane for improved signal integrity

Design Process

1. Schematic design
2. Component selection
3. Footprint assignment
4. PCB layout
5. Component placement
6. Signal and power routing
7. Ground-plane design
8. Design Rule Check (DRC)
9. 3D PCB verification

PCB Design Considerations

- USB data lines were routed carefully.
- Power and ground traces were designed for reliable operation.
- Protection components were included at the USB interface.
- Component placement was optimized for a compact layout.
- PCB clearances and design rules were verified using KiCad DRC.

